# WhatsApp Chat Viewer - Cursor AI Rules

## Project Context
This is a Spring Boot application for parsing and managing WhatsApp chat exports. Users upload zipped chat files, and the system stores chat entries in a database and multimedia files in a separate file system.

## Critical Security Rules
- ALWAYS include userId parameter in all database queries and service methods
- NEVER allow cross-user data access - users can only access their own data
- ALWAYS validate user ownership before any data operation
- All repository methods must include userId as the first parameter
- All service methods must verify user ownership

## Code Standards
- Use Java 21+ features
- Use Spring Boot 3.x
- Use Lombok for reducing boilerplate
- Follow Java naming conventions
- Include Javadoc for public methods
- Use snake_case for database tables and columns

## Database Rules
- All queries must be user-scoped (include userId)
- Use pagination for large result sets
- Include proper indexes for performance
- Use created_at and updated_at timestamps
- Use soft deletes with status field

## File Storage
- Multimedia files are stored separately from database
- File names are based on SHA256 hash of content
- Hierarchical directory structure: hash.substring(0,3)/hash.substring(3,6)/hash
- Support multiple storage providers (local, NFS, S3, GCP)

## API Design
- Use RESTful principles
- Include API versioning in URL path
- Always support pagination for list endpoints
- Use consistent error response format
- Use kebab-case for URLs

## Testing Requirements
- Write unit tests for all service methods
- Write integration tests for API endpoints
- Include security tests for user isolation
- Test performance for large datasets

## Error Handling
- Use consistent exception types
- Provide user-friendly error messages
- Include appropriate logging
- Never expose internal system details

## Performance Considerations
- Support up to 50,000 users
- Each user can have up to 1,000 chats
- Sub-second response times for searches
- Use database connection pooling
- Implement proper indexing strategy

## When reviewing or generating code:
1. Always check for userId inclusion in database operations
2. Verify user isolation is maintained
3. Ensure proper error handling
4. Check for performance implications
5. Validate security boundaries
6. Include appropriate logging
7. Follow naming conventions
8. Add necessary tests